Deploy a web application in Azure
Step 1: Build your web application on your local machine and keep the code ready.

Step 2: Login to Azure Portal and create a Storage Account (if you don’t already have one).

Step 3: Open the Storage Account
Go to:
Data Management → Static website
Enable Static website hosting.

Step 4: Go to:
Containers → $web
Upload all your source code files (HTML, CSS, JS).

Step 5:
Go back to Static website page and copy the website URL.
Use that URL to access your deployed web app.
